the good times are looking even farther away for enron . the company ' s inability to extend its energy - trading model to some other commodities is proving increasingly costly . on oct . 16 , the nation ' s top natural - gas trader and leading wholesale electricity marketer reported a $ 1 . 01 billion charge . among other things , that covers recent forays into broadband and water trading - - as well as the unraveling of a pair of limited partnerships . those partnerships had raised questions about conflicts of interest . until recently , they had been overseen by the company ' s cfo , andrew fastow , even though they were outside entities that bought assets from enron . the aftertax charge was one reason the company posted a $ 618 million loss in the third quarter , vs . a profit of $ 292 million in the year - ago period . without the charge , enron would have shown a profit of $ 393 million for the quarter .
